e 31st of October no  ifs no buts and then focusing on that  really important domestic agenda I just  say to Stephen yeah I knock on doors  like all my colleagues week after week  out there in in the doorsteps of of  certainly reading what people want to  see is for us to get brexit done to get  that out of the way and then to refocus  on the issues that matter to them on a  day to day basis and that is more police  more funding for schools more money for  the frontline the NHS and that is what  the Prime Minister's already set out and  we will see further announcements I'm  sure at the spending review on Wednesday  and yet all this whole argument around  brexit and the side that one was about  taking back control and about this huge  piece of democracy that we put in place  about getting back sovereignty for the  United Kingdom and the UK Parliament  this is removing so whether you you  think this is you know of  thirty-five days or whether it's just  four or five days in in real terms at  Parliament isn't going to be sitting the  reality is it is removing some of the  say that parliamentarians can have on  this issue how is that a democratic move  well I would disagree with that we've  had three years of discussion of our own  brexit there is time for more discussion  around brexit and also it's  fundamentally it's worth remembering  that the European Council will take  place in the middle of October so you  know we won't know whether there is a  deal we certainly want to deal that's  what the Prime Minister has set out very  clearly we want to have a deal but we  won't know that the details of that  until the 18th of October as I said  there's plenty time after that to debate  not just the domestic agenda but also  any future deal when it comes to brexit  you mentioned plenty of time before as  well these additional days that we've  got before me next week is going to be a  very busy week for you all if it does  get through the House of Commons that  you if they 